#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:4
msgid "Step 3: Collecting Coverage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:6
msgid ""
"This step extends :ref:`Step 2 <CTest Dashboard Step 2>` by collecting code "
"coverage and submitting it to CDash.  It does not enable the build error "
"from Step 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:10
msgid "Step3/submit.cmake"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:10
msgid ""
"set(CTEST_BUILD_NAME \"Step3: coverage\")\n"
"site_name(CTEST_SITE)\n"
"set(CTEST_SOURCE_DIRECTORY \"${CTEST_SCRIPT_DIRECTORY}/../Project\")\n"
"set(CTEST_BINARY_DIRECTORY \"${CTEST_SCRIPT_DIRECTORY}/build\")\n"
"set(CTEST_CMAKE_GENERATOR \"Unix Makefiles\")\n"
"set(CTEST_NOTES_FILES \"${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_FILE}\")\n"
"\n"
"set(CTEST_UPDATE_COMMAND \"git\")\n"
"set(CTEST_UPDATE_VERSION_ONLY 1)\n"
"\n"
"set(CTEST_USE_LAUNCHERS 1)\n"
"\n"
"# Tell CTest to use gcov for coverage analysis.\n"
"set(CTEST_COVERAGE_COMMAND \"gcov\")\n"
"\n"
"ctest_empty_binary_directory(\"${CTEST_BINARY_DIRECTORY}\")\n"
"\n"
"ctest_start(Experimental)\n"
"ctest_update()\n"
"\n"
"# Build with the --coverage flag to enable gcov-style instrumentation.\n"
"set(options\n"
"  \"-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug\"\n"
"  \"-DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=--coverage\"\n"
"  )\n"
"ctest_configure(OPTIONS \"${options}\")\n"
"\n"
"ctest_build()\n"
"ctest_test()\n"
"\n"
"# Run gcov to find which lines of code the tests executed.\n"
"ctest_coverage()\n"
"\n"
"ctest_submit()\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:14
msgid "Two things are needed to collect coverage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:16
msgid ""
"Build the project with instrumentation.  The ``--coverage`` flag makes GCC "
"and Clang add counters that record which lines run.  A ``Debug`` build "
"avoids optimizations that would make the line counts less accurate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:21
msgid ""
"Run the coverage tool.  After :command:`ctest_test`, "
"the :command:`ctest_coverage` command runs the tool given "
"by :variable:`CTEST_COVERAGE_COMMAND` on the data the tests produced. CTest "
"parses its output and submits the coverage of each file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:26
msgid ""
"On CDash, the build shows the overall coverage percentage.  The details show "
"the coverage of each file, with the lines that ran and the lines that did "
"not.  For example, the ``fails`` test never runs one line of ``fails.cxx``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:31
msgid "Project/fails.cxx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:31
msgid ""
"#include <iostream>\n"
"\n"
"int main()\n"
"{\n"
"  bool b = false;\n"
"  if (b) {\n"
"    // This line never runs, so coverage reports it as missed.\n"
"    std::cout << \"this shouldn't happen...\" << std::endl;\n"
"  }\n"
"\n"
"  std::cout << \"this test fails\" << std::endl;\n"
"  return 1;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:36
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:38
msgid ""
"GCC or Clang (supports ``--coverage`` / ``-fprofile-arcs -ftest-coverage``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:39
msgid ""
"A ``gcov`` tool that matches the compiler version, found in the ``PATH``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:41
msgid "See the :ref:`CTest Coverage Step` for other supported tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:44
msgid "Running the Script"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Collecting Coverage.rst:46
msgid "ctest -S Step3/submit.cmake -V"
msgstr ""
